# Line-ending policy for hash-verified artifacts.
#
# artifacts.lock.json records a byte size and sha256 for every artifact it
# manages. Git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout, which changes those bytes and makes bootstrap.py report intact files
# as corrupt. Observed on config.mstcn_553_ff_thresholds: 804 bytes on the
# cluster, 818 in a Windows clone, byte-identical after normalising line endings
# — the deployed model's frozen calibration reported INVALID for no real reason.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion so these check out byte-identical to
# what was committed and hashed.
#
# Scoped deliberately to evidence paths. A blanket rule (e.g. *.jsonl) also
# catches the vendored LLMDet/llava/ trees and makes 400+ unrelated files look
# modified, which buries the artifacts this is meant to protect.

# HPC evidence: metrics, tables, calibration, run records, predictions
LLMDet/work_dirs/** -text

# The lock itself
artifacts.lock.json -text

# Project data and annotations whose bytes are referenced or hashed
event_gold_bundle/** -text
grounding_data/** -text
outputs/** -text
reports/** -text

# Binary artifacts: never convert, and do not attempt text diffs
*.pth    -text -diff
*.pt     -text -diff
*.npz    -text -diff
*.npy    -text -diff
*.tflite -text -diff
*.task   -text -diff

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they fail on the cluster with
# "/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter"
*.sh text eol=lf
